From 6ce3864c072815c1e756280f710de3cfc0aabc89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:31:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Canonical session status envelope: backend reducer,
 strict readers, fenced publication (slice L2a)

Backend half of the approved single-status plan (card t_7a017359ecef3767, approved plan dispositions
14/15/15a/16). Cut from fresh main as a minimal slice; replaces the omnibus branch of PR #3852.
The Desktop half (paint only this envelope, committed-paint reports, drift) is the next commit (L2b).

Why
- The sidebar flapped done/grey because a Desktop-local fetch-completeness veto overrode the backend
  outcome, and the backend chose its status from a prose heuristic after informational notice rows
  invalidated declarations. There was no single revisioned status the surfaces could agree on.

What
- hermes_state_session_status.py (new, pure): reduce one qualified snapshot to
  {status_version=1, identity, generation, revision, source_revisions, coverage, failures, kind,
  presentation{stripe, reason_codes}}. Precedence: mute; genuine human ask; own active turn; open
  linked work; unknown/failed/lost evidence (never green); settled owning turn + all work terminal =
  done; never-started draft = no stripe. A failure persists until a later generation's own successful
  completion.
- hermes_state_session_status_snapshot.py (new): collects that snapshot over the EXISTING readers
  (cards, registered control providers, turn lease/marker/routing tokens, subagents, goals) and the
  strict process inventory, each read strictly: a reader that raises is unknown coverage for that
  source (reason code <source>_read_failed:<Error>), never an empty list. refresh_outcome stores the
  envelope under outcome_json["status"]; sessions.outcome_json stays the single persisted status, no
  new table, column, poller or trigger.
- No prose heuristic, summary judge or declaration selects the envelope. A declaration keeps the
  stored envelope instead of resetting it (revision stays monotonic) and is explanation only.
- Generation = newest genuine user request. Provenance-validated informational notices and completion
  notes (existing settled_notice / outcome_informational / completion_note proof) do not start one and
  do not reopen a done session; any other user row (typed, steered, folded, unproven) does.
- Turn settlement (disposition 15/15a): a turn observed with ownership tokens settles only on a
  turn_end naming one of them; otherwise unknown(turn_unsettled), never green. The newest admission
  decides. A generation never observed with tokens keeps main's transcript reading (no schema, no
  request/response receipt).
- tools/process_registry{,_results}.py: opt-in strict, session-qualified load_completed_results /
  list_sessions(include_retained=True): enumeration, decode, owner-scope and missing-exit errors
  propagate instead of being swallowed; nothing is pruned on a strict read. Default tool/display
  behaviour is unchanged.
- Publication is compare-and-set on the stored outcome text and the newest user row, with bounded
  retries: a stale collector re-collects against its successor and never overwrites it. A failed read
  is published as a source_unknown revision; the next successful refresh recovers.

Existing tests touched (3 assertions lines added, no expected value of an existing field changed):
- tests/hermes_state/test_session_outcome.py::test_5_declared_done_holds_until_a_newer_user_row,
  ::test_busy_card_read_cannot_derive_done, tests/hermes_state/test_session_outcome_subagent_lost.py::
  test_a_declared_done_after_its_last_activity_accounts_for_it compared the whole returned dict; they
  now pop the additive "status" key first (and assert it: unread board = unknown, plan line 24;
  declared content unchanged, plan line 20).

Proof (canonical runner, HERMES_TEST_FILE_RETRIES=0)
- RED first: tests/hermes_state/test_session_status_refresh.py 0 passed / 25 failed before the code.
- GREEN: 65 files, 1338 passed, 0 failed: the new real-entry-point file (25), reducer (76), strict
  process reader (14) and every test file referencing hermes_state_outcome / refresh_outcome /
  outcome_json / turn_outcome / process_registry_results.

Known limits
- The surrounding outcome's legacy top-level kind/summary is still derived as before for non-Desktop
  consumers (cron release, CLI text); only the envelope is canonical. Desktop moves to it in L2b.
- A revision certifies one pass over the readers, not cross-source atomicity.
- Processes that predate the registry's retention window are not counted (not a claim of success).
  Live processes are read from this interpreter's registry plus retained receipts; exhaustive
  cross-interpreter checkpoint recovery is not claimed. Hosted sandbox scopes read as unknown.
- Tokenless legacy turns keep main's transcript reading: no regression vs main, no new attribution.
- Ended delegate children are not enumerated as affirmative successes (as on main).
- If every bounded publication attempt meets a successor's write, the successor's value stands and a
  warning is logged; that refresh publishes nothing.
- Not yet proven here: installed Desktop parity rows 1-6 (needs L2b, ship and install).
- Read-only replay of the envelope over a copy of this host's real state.db (60 newest sessions, 0
  errors) found one real race before this commit: a receipt pruned by another producer between
  enumeration and read raised FileNotFoundError and read as unknown. A vanished receipt is now expiry
  in strict reads too (2 RED-first tests); other read errors still propagate.
- A non-zero or killed process exit reads as attention until the next request completes (disposition
  15), including exits the agent caused itself.
